# [The Landing Party](landing_party)

Erebus Station has not answered in nineteen hours. It sits on the inner moon of the gas
giant Kaleth, four people aboard, studying the cloud deck.

Everything below is content. The mission script reacts to it and holds no story of its
own: the cast becomes lifeforms, the scenes become the beats each console plays, and the
four `signal` outcomes are the only things the script counts.

The shape to keep if this is edited: **every location offers each character something
only they can do, and nobody can take all four.** The story is legible only when the
party puts its readings together, which is the whole reason it is played by four people
at four consoles instead of one person with a menu.

## [Boarding Party](team)

The bodies on the ground. One per console. `Roles` is what the scene guards read, so
every gated choice below names one of these words.

### [Dr Sorel](sorel)
---
Face: terran_female
Roles: boarding, medical
Color: "#4cf"
---
Ship's surgeon. Reads bodies. Has signed more death certificates than she has opinions.

### [Chief Ruiz](ruiz)
---
Face: terran_male
Roles: boarding, engineering
Color: "#fc4"
---
Engineer. Reads machines, and trusts them further than he trusts the people running them.

### [Ensign Vale](vale)
---
Face: terran_male
Roles: boarding, security
Color: "#f66"
---
Security. Reads rooms. Youngest person on the team and the only one carrying anything.

### [Lt Anders](anders)
---
Face: terran_fluid
Roles: boarding, science
Color: "#8f8"
---
Science officer. Reads records. Would rather be right slowly than first.

## [Voices](voices)

Not people on the team. These are voices the scenes may name without a body being spawned
for them, because the mission builds lifeforms from `## Boarding Party` only.

### [Erebus](outpost)
---
Face: terran_fluid
Roles: narrator
Color: "#aaa"
---
The station itself, and the flat voice of what you are looking at.

### [Dr Haruki](haruki)
---
Face: terran_female
Roles: narrator
Color: "#fd8"
---
Senior researcher. Alive, in the shelter, and not sorry.

## [Hails](hails)

What arrives when the ship takes orbit. Beaming down is a DECISION the captain makes on
the comms, not something that happens to the crew because they flew somewhere.

The choices here are evaluated against the SHIP, not against a boarding character, so they
carry no role guards - the per character menus start once the team is on the ground.

### [Something Is Still Transmitting](orbit_call)
---
Speaker: outpost
Title: Erebus Beacon
Presentation: orbit
Subject: gasgiant
Color: "#aaa"
---
% Carrier only, on the survey band, cycling every ninety seconds. Under it there is about a second of voice.
% It is too short to be a message and too regular to be an accident, and it has been doing this for nineteen hours.

- [Clean it up and play it again](orbit_repeat)
- [Assemble a boarding party]()
- [Hold position and keep scanning]()

### [The Second Left of It](orbit_repeat)
---
Speaker: outpost
Title: Erebus Beacon
Presentation: orbit
Subject: gasgiant
Color: "#aaa"
---
% One voice, one word, and the word is "cold". Then the carrier again.
% Whoever recorded it set it to repeat and then did not come back to say anything else.

- [Assemble a boarding party]()
- [Hold position and keep scanning]()

## [Scenes](boarding)

Four locations, then a decision. At each location every character can read one thing, and
what they read is theirs alone; the four readings only add up if the party says them out
loud to each other.

Four facts are worth having, and each can be reached more than one way, so no single route
through the station is the correct one:

| Signal | What the party now knows |
|---|---|
| `lp_cold` | The station is losing heat faster than it can make it. |
| `lp_gentle` | It touches. It has not struck at anything. |
| `lp_willing` | Nothing was forced. The crew opened every door themselves. |
| `lp_sample` | It came up from the cloud deck, in a jar, logged as non motile. |

Three of the four unlock the ending that is not a weapon.

**Each fact is awarded in exactly two places, and no location gives more than two.** That
is a balance, not an accident: a party has to move through the station rather than strip
one room, and there is no single correct route. If a reading is moved, move its pair too.

### [Entry Corridor](arrival)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% The inner hatch stands open. The lights are down to their night cycle and nothing is moving.
% Your breath is visible. That is the first thing anyone notices, and nobody says it yet.

- [Kneel by the body at the hatch](arrival_med) if medical >= 1 ; signal lp_gentle
- [Read the corridor thermals](arrival_eng) if engineering >= 1 ; signal lp_cold
- [Check how this hatch was opened](arrival_sec) if security >= 1
- [Pull the last transmission](arrival_sci) if science >= 1
- [Move further in](lab)

### [The Body at the Hatch](arrival_med)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% Not a fall and not a weapon. The burn is contact, and it wraps the forearm the way a grip would.
% Whatever held him was warm enough to blister the suit liner, and it held on for some time.

- [Say it out loud](arrival)

### [The Corridor Thermals](arrival_eng)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% Four degrees, in a corridor rated for twenty. Every heater on this deck is at maximum.
% They are not broken. They are losing, and they have been losing for most of a day.

- [Say it out loud](arrival)

### [The Hatch Mechanism](arrival_sec)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% No cutting, no forcing, no override. The manual lever is thrown, from this side.
% Somebody stood here, in the cold, and opened the door on purpose.

- [Say it out loud](arrival)

### [The Last Transmission](arrival_sci)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% It stops between sentences, not between words. Nobody was interrupted.
% The last thing Erebus said to anyone was that they would call back after the next observation.

- [Say it out loud](arrival)

### [The Sample Lab](lab)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% Two workstations, both logged in. A jacket over a chair back. It is colder in here than the corridor.
% The containment cabinet is open and the light inside it is still on.

- [Examine the containment gel](lab_med) if medical >= 1
- [Check why containment failed](lab_eng) if engineering >= 1 ; signal lp_willing
- [Read the room](lab_sec) if security >= 1
- [Pull the sample manifest](lab_sci) if science >= 1 ; signal lp_sample
- [Go down to the reactor gallery](gallery)

### [The Containment Gel](lab_med)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% Body temperature, near enough, and it should be at minus forty. Something has been keeping it warm.
% There are no cells in it. Nothing in this gel has ever divided.

- [Say it out loud](lab)

### [Why Containment Failed](lab_eng)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% It did not fail. The field was switched off, from the panel, in the correct order, one interlock at a time.
% Whoever did it took their time and did it properly.

- [Say it out loud](lab)

### [Reading the Lab](lab_sec)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% No overturned chair, no dropped tools, nothing thrown. Two cups of coffee, both stone cold, both nearly full.
% Nobody in this room was ever in a hurry.

- [Say it out loud](lab)

### [The Sample Manifest](lab_sci)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% Recovered from the cloud deck at nine hundred millibars. Mass, four kilograms. Classification, non motile.
% Somebody has written a question mark beside the classification, in pencil, some time later.

- [Say it out loud](lab)

### [Reactor Gallery](gallery)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% It is wrapped around the coolant loop, three decks of it, and it is the colour of a bruise under ice.
% It knows you are here. Nothing about it moves toward you.

- [Watch it breathe](gallery_med) if medical >= 1
- [Read the coolant loop](gallery_eng) if engineering >= 1 ; signal lp_cold
- [Hold the doorway and watch it](gallery_sec) if security >= 1
- [Match it against the cloud deck survey](gallery_sci) if science >= 1 ; signal lp_sample
- [Go up to the shelter](shelter)

### [Watching It Breathe](gallery_med)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% There is a rhythm in it, slow and getting slower, and you have seen that rhythm before in things that were failing.
% If this is dying, it is dying of cold, in the warmest room on the station.

- [Say it out loud](gallery)

### [The Coolant Loop](gallery_eng)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% The loop is running backwards. It is not venting heat, it is being drained of it, and the reactor is answering by burning harder.
% At this rate the station has about four hours of fuel and then it has none.

- [Say it out loud](gallery)

### [Holding the Doorway](gallery_sec)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% You have stood in the open for ninety seconds. It has had ninety seconds.
% Whatever it did to the man at the hatch, it is not doing to you, and it could.

- [Say it out loud](gallery)

### [The Cloud Deck Survey](gallery_sci)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% Same spectrum as the sample, and the same as the band it was lifted from. This is not a thing that came here.
% This is a thing that was brought here, and the pressure it likes is a hundred kilometres below your boots.

- [Say it out loud](gallery)

### [The Shelter](shelter)
---
Speaker: haruki
---
% Three of us. We have been in here since it got out, and we are not hiding from it.
% We are keeping out of its way, which is a different thing, and I would like somebody to write that down correctly.

- [Examine the survivors](shelter_med) if medical >= 1
- [Ask what they routed the power to](shelter_eng) if engineering >= 1
- [Check how this door was secured](shelter_sec) if security >= 1 ; signal lp_willing
- [Ask Haruki what she thinks it is](shelter_sci) if science >= 1 ; signal lp_gentle
- [Decide what to do](decide)

### [The Survivors](shelter_med)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% Hypothermic, all three, and the youngest is badly so. Not one of them is burned.
% They have been losing heat for a day and none of them has been touched.

- [Say it out loud](shelter)

### [Where the Power Went](shelter_eng)
---
Speaker: haruki
---
% Every watt we could spare, into the heater in the far cabin, and then we shut the door on it.
% Not a trap. Somewhere warm that is not where the people are. It went, and it stayed.

- [Say it out loud](shelter)

### [The Shelter Door](shelter_sec)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% Barricaded from inside, with lockers, in a hurry. The lock itself was never engaged.
% They built a wall they could climb over and left the door unlocked behind it.

- [Say it out loud](shelter)

### [Haruki's Answer](shelter_sci)
---
Speaker: haruki
---
% It followed the heat. Every time. Never the people, and we were the warmest things in the room for the first hour.
% Marchetti got in the way of the heat, at the hatch. That is all that happened to Marchetti.

- [Say it out loud](shelter)

### [What We Do](decide)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% Four hours of fuel, three people who cannot take another cold night, and a thing on the coolant loop that has not once come at you.
% Whatever gets decided in this corridor is going in somebody's report.

- [Vent the gallery and open the flue to the cloud deck](ending_home) if briefed >= 1 ; signal lp_end_home
- [Burn it off the coolant loop](ending_burn) ; signal lp_end_burn
- [Ask the survivors what they want](decide_ask)

### [Asking the Survivors](decide_ask)
---
Speaker: haruki
---
% You are asking the wrong question and you are asking it of the wrong people. Ask what it is doing, not what it is.
% We have had a day to work that out and we did not manage it either, so I would not be proud of the delay.

- [Back to it](decide)

### [The Long Way Down](ending_home)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% You cut the gallery open to the sky and let the pressure fall, and it goes, the way water goes down a drain, unhurried.
% Ninety kilometres below, the cloud deck takes it back. The heaters catch up by morning. Haruki writes down what it did, correctly.

- [Beam back up]()

### [The Short Way](ending_burn)
---
Speaker: outpost
---
% It comes off the loop in about forty seconds and it does not fight at any point during them.
% The station is warm again by the end of the watch. Nobody in the shelter says anything to you, and Haruki files her own report.

- [Beam back up]()
